 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Two parables of this world (worldly fire, rain, lightning). The fire undraws at «بنورهم». No eye or ear motif (18, 19, 20). Short-word flag 20:12 to check by ear. STAGING v4: 17-18 (parable): one man kindles a worldly fire on a dark night, it goes out on «ذهب» (before the Name) and the scene darkens on «وتركهم»; only the kindler is drawn (Muyassar speaks of a group, As-Sa'di of the man). 19-20 (parable): an uncountable group walking in the open (Muyassar: جماعة يمشون في العراء) in heavy rain, darkness and lightning; they walk when it lights (20:8) and stop when it darkens (20:11). No fingers-in-ears gesture, no eye or ear motif; nothing on the Name."
 },
